# Project Layout

High-level project folder layout.

/
├─ apps/                                - Next.js apps that primarily consume the packages
│  ├─ sda/                              - Single DAO App (frontend for a single DAO)
│  │  ├─ pages/                         - Next.js pages
│  ├─ dapp/                             - DAO App (primary multi-DAO frontend)
│  │  ├─ pages/                         - Next.js pages
├─ packages/                            - Packages that are shared between apps
│  ├─ config/                           - Configuration for various packages
│  │  ├─ eslint/                        - ESLint config
│  │  ├─ prettier/                      - Prettier config
│  │  ├─ tailwind/                      - Tailwind config
│  │  ├─ ts/                            - TypeScript config
│  │  ├─ vitest/                        - Vitest config
│  ├─ dispatch/                         - Dispatch control center for managing operations
│  │  ├─ deploy/                        - Deployment control center scripts
│  │  ├─ polytone/                      - Polytone control center scripts
│  ├─ email/                            - Email template management
│  ├─ i18n/                             - Internationalization
│  │  ├─ locales/                       - Translation files
│  │  │  ├─ en/                         - English translations
│  │  │  │  ├─ translation.json         - Common translations
│  ├─ math/                             - Math utilities
│  ├─ state/                            - State management, no UI
│  │  ├─ clients/                       - Native clients for creating and interacting with DAOs, proposal modules, and voting modules, following shared interfaces for interoperability
│  │  ├─ contracts/                     - Autogenerated execution and query clients for contracts
│  │  ├─ graphql/                       - GraphQL queries
│  │  ├─ indexer/                       - Indexer clients and functions
│  │  ├─ query/                         - React Query queries that do not depend on stateful features
│  │  ├─ recoil/                        - Recoil state management that does not depend on stateful features
│  │  ├─ utils/                         - Utilities that depend on state
│  ├─ stateful/                         - Stateful components, hooks, and features that integrate state (from the state package) and UI (from the stateless package)—this is the synthesis layer where everything comes together
│  │  ├─ actions/                       - Clients and components for DAO Actions
│  │  ├─ command/                       - Clients and components for the Command modal
│  │  ├─ components/                    - Stateful React components
│  │  ├─ creators/                      - Components and logic for DAO creator flows
│  │  ├─ feed/                          - Components and logic for the DAO feed on the home page
│  │  ├─ hooks/                         - Stateful React hooks
│  │  ├─ modules/                       - Modules that can be used in DAOs
│  │  ├─ proposal-module-adapter/       - Components and logic for the various proposal modules
│  │  ├─ recoil/                        - Recoil state management that depends on other stateful features
│  │  ├─ voting-module-adapter/         - Components and logic for the various voting modules
│  │  ├─ server/                        - Server-side code for the apps
│  ├─ stateless/                        - Stateless components, hooks, and features that do not depend on state
│  │  ├─ actions/                       - Clients to handle encoding and decoding of actions, as well as the base action interface
│  │  ├─ components/                    - Stateless React components
│  │  ├─ contexts/                      - React contexts for various sets of data
│  │  ├─ hooks/                         - Stateless React hooks
│  │  ├─ pages/                         - Stateless Next.js pages
│  │  ├─ providers/                     - React providers for the contexts
│  │  ├─ styles/                        - CSS styles
│  │  ├─ theme/                         - Theme management context
│  ├─ storybook/                        - Storybook decorators and config
│  ├─ tests/                            - Vitest integration tests
│  ├─ types/                            - TypeScript types
│  │  ├─ clients/                       - TypeScript types for the native clients
│  │  ├─ components/                    - TypeScript types for the React components
│  │  ├─ contracts/                     - TypeScript types for the autogenerated contract clients
│  │  ├─ protobuf/                      - Autogenerated protobuf type definitions
│  ├─ utils/                            - Utilities, mostly functions
│  │  ├─ api/                           - Next.js API functions to be used in apps
│  │  ├─ constants/                     - Constants, environment variables, etc.
│  │  │  ├─ codeIds.json                - The deployed code IDs for each chain and version
│  │  ├─ messages/                      - CosmWasm and protobuf message encoding/decoding utilities
│  │  ├─ scripts/                       - Development scripts
│  │  ├─ secret/                        - Secret Network utilities
│  │  ├─ server/                        - Server-side utilities
│  │  ├─ validation/                    - Form validation functions

## Package Interdependency Restrictions

### Apps

Apps can depend on any package.

### Packages

All packages can depend on `config`, `math`, `types`, and `utils`.

#### `config`

No interdependencies allowed.

#### `i18n`

No other interdependencies allowed.

#### `math`

No other interdependencies allowed.

#### `state`

Can only depend on `math`, `utils`, `config`, and `types`.

#### `stateful`

Can depend on any package. Nothing can depend on `stateful` except for `apps`.

#### `stateless`

Can only depend on `math`, `config`, `types`, and `utils`.

#### `types`

Can only depend on `math` and `config`.

#### `utils`

Can only depend on `math`, `config`, and `types`.
